import FormalSchemes.TateInvNodeChartInvariant

set_option linter.style.header false

/-!
# Hypothesis 4 of the node chart's four: what the descent being an isomorphism actually says

`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_formalScheme_of_isIso_desc_nodeChartAdicHom`
(`FormalSchemes.TateInvNodeChartInvariant`) leaves exactly one obligation. Over a principal base
ideal generated by a non-zero-divisor, `T_inv/⟨σ⟩` is a formal scheme as soon as

```
(isActionQuotient_actionQuotientπ (tateInvNodeChartRestrictedAction …)).desc
  (nodeChartAdicHom …) (isActionInvariant_nodeChartAdicHom …)
```

is an isomorphism. Hypotheses 1 and 3 are proved (`adicSectionsLocallyFG_nodeChartPsi`,
`isActionInvariant_nodeChartAdicHom`) and the overlap condition is not a hypothesis at all since
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalScheme.AdicSectionsLocallyFG.overlapAdic`. This file takes the last one
apart. It does **not** decide it.

## The packaging comes off, and what is left when it has

`CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.isIso_desc_iff` (`FormalSchemes.ActionQuotient`) says a mediating
morphism is an isomorphism exactly when the invariant morphism it descends is *itself* a quotient
projection. Applied here that is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_desc_nodeChartAdicHom_iff_isActionQuotient`: hypothesis 4 says nothing
about the coequalizer object, only

> `AlgebraicGeometry.nodeChartAdicHom` exhibits `Spf (tateInvNodeChartQuotientIdeal …)` as the
> quotient of the saturated node-chart locus by the restricted `σ`-action.

Because the right-hand side names no quotient object, the condition cannot depend on which
presentation of the quotient the descent was taken along
(`CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.isIso_desc_iff_isIso_desc`). Descending along
`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.restrictπ` instead of along the coequalizer therefore gives
the same condition at a morphism out of an honest open of `T_inv/⟨σ⟩`:

> `AlgebraicGeometry.nodeChartQuotientHom : (T_inv/⟨σ⟩)|_{V₀} ⟶ Spf (Γ (T_inv/⟨σ⟩, V₀))`,
> the unique morphism with `restrictπ ≫ nodeChartQuotientHom = nodeChartAdicHom`,

and `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_desc_nodeChartAdicHom_iff` says hypothesis 4 is exactly that this is
an isomorphism. What comes off is the descent packaging: neither
`CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.desc` nor the coequalizer of the restricted action occurs in it.
What does not come off, checked on the elaborated statement rather than read off the source:
`CategoryTheory.actionQuotient` still occurs, at the *period* action, because the source is an open
of `T_inv/⟨σ⟩` itself and that is the object in question, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalScheme.AdicSectionsLocallyFG` still occurs, as the type of the witness the
morphism is built from. In words: **the node chart's open of the quotient is the formal spectrum
of its own ring of sections, via the canonical comparison.**

`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_formalScheme_of_isIso_nodeChartQuotientHom` restates the headline over
that morphism.

## The two halves, and which one is discharged

`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.isIso_iff_isIso_base_and_isIso_c_app`
(`FormalSchemes.ActionQuotientRestrictQuotient`) splits it into the base map and the comparison
maps on sections, in both directions, so a refutation of either half refutes hypothesis 4. That is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_desc_nodeChartAdicHom_iff_base_and_c`:

* the **space half** — the continuous map from `V₀ ⊆ T_inv/⟨σ⟩` to
  `FormalSpectrum (tateInvNodeChartQuotientIdeal …)` is a homeomorphism;
* the **sheaf half** — for every open `U` of that formal spectrum, the comparison
  `Γ (Spf …, U) ⟶ Γ ((T_inv/⟨σ⟩)|_{V₀}, f ⁻¹ U)` is an isomorphism of rings.

**The sheaf half is discharged at `U = ⊤`**, unconditionally:
`AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_c_app_top_nodeChartQuotientHom`. The route is
`AlgebraicGeometry.globalSectionsHom_nodeChartQuotientHom`, which computes the global-sections
homomorphism of the descent to be the canonical identification
`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.restrictTopSectionsIso`, using only that
`AlgebraicGeometry.nodeChartAdicHom` induces `AlgebraicGeometry.nodeChartPsi` on global sections
(`AlgebraicGeometry.globalSectionsHom_nodeChartAdicHom`), that `nodeChartPsi` is the pullback of
sections along the projection (`AlgebraicGeometry.nodeChartSectionsHom_eq_restrictπ`), and that a
section of a quotient is determined by its pullback
(`CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.injective_c_app`).

**This is a structural discharge and not progress on the geometry, and it should not be read as
one.** No property of the node locus, of the annulus algebras or of the `σ`-action enters; the
morphism was *built* from `nodeChartPsi`, so its global-sections comparison could hardly be
anything else. What it buys is a narrowing: the content of hypothesis 4 is entirely in the base map
and in the sheaf comparison at the *proper* opens of the formal spectrum.

## Main definitions and results

* `CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.globalSectionsHom_desc_eq`: the global-sections homomorphism of
  a descent is pinned by that of the morphism descended, because a quotient projection is injective
  on sections.
* `FormalSpectrum.isIso_c_app_top_of_bijective_globalSectionsHom`: a morphism into a formal
  spectrum whose global-sections homomorphism is bijective has an invertible comparison map at `⊤`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.nodeChartSectionsHom_eq_restrictπ`: the node chart's section map is the
  pullback along `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.restrictπ`, read through
  `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.restrictTopSectionsIso`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.nodeChartQuotientHom` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.restrictπ_comp_nodeChartQuotientHom`: the descent along the restricted
  projection, and its defining factorisation.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_desc_nodeChartAdicHom_iff_isActionQuotient`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_desc_nodeChartAdicHom_iff`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_desc_nodeChartAdicHom_iff_base_and_c`: **the reductions.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.globalSectionsHom_nodeChartQuotientHom` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_c_app_top_nodeChartQuotientHom`: the sheaf half at `⊤`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_formalScheme_of_isIso_nodeChartQuotientHom`: the headline restated over
  the canonical comparison.

## What is *not* proved here

**`hnode` is undecided, in both directions, and nothing here moves it.** The score of
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_formalScheme_of_adicSections` after this file is unchanged: hypothesis 1
proved, the overlap condition a theorem rather than a component, hypothesis 3 proved, **hypothesis
4 open**. No witness of hypothesis 4 is produced, and no argument that one exists is given.

**Refuting hypothesis 4 would not refute `hnode`.** The hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_formalScheme_of_isIso_desc` is *existential* — some invariant morphism
whose descent is an isomorphism — and hypothesis 4 is that condition at a **named** morphism, so it
implies the existential and is a priori stronger. The chain onward through
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_formalScheme_of_iso_restrict_tateInvNodeChartQuotientOpens` discharges a
containment of ranges and is one-way as well. Everything below is a restatement of hypothesis 4 and
inherits both facts.

**Neither half is decided.** For the space half, the only description of
`AlgebraicGeometry.nodeChartAdicHom` on points that exists is chart-by-chart
(`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalScheme.chart_comp_homOfGlobalSectionsHomOfAdicSections`), and
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalScheme.AdicSectionsLocallyFG.chart` is `Classical.choice`, so no
computation of the base map is available on this tree; what a decision needs is the primes of
`AlgebraicGeometry.tateInvNodeChartQuotientIdeal`'s ring, which is a statement about the invariant
sections of the chain and not a general fact. For the sheaf half at a proper open `U`, what is
needed is that `Γ (Spf …, U)` agrees with the invariant sections of the chain over the preimage of
`U` — by `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.exists_c_app_restrictπ_eq_iff_isInvariantSection`
the right-hand side of the comparison *is* those invariant sections — and that is the computation
`FormalSchemes.TateInvNodeChartQuotientOpen` carries out at `V₀` itself, at a proper open. **So the
space half is blocked by there being no handle on the base map, and the sheaf half by a
Tate-specific section computation.** Neither of those sentences is asserted by a declaration below;
they are a reading of what is present, and the reader should check it against
`AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_desc_nodeChartAdicHom_iff_base_and_c` rather than take it.

**Nothing here bears on `AlgebraicGeometry.tateInvNodeChartAmbientHom`.**
`AlgebraicGeometry.not_isOpenImmersion_tateInvNodeChartAmbientHom_of_ne_top` refutes it as an open
immersion and that refutation is untouched, as is `FormalSchemes.TateInvNodeChartAmbient`'s record
that `AlgebraicGeometry.tateInvNodeChartAwayIdeal` is not shown to be an ideal of definition. The
morphism reduced to below has a different source and a different target and no relation to it is
proved.

**Nothing here bears on `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.IsFreeProperlyDiscontinuous` for the
period action**, which `AlgebraicGeometry.not_isFreeProperlyDiscontinuous_tateInvPeriodAction`
refutes globally.

## Implementation notes

`CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.isIso_desc_iff` and
`CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.isIso_desc_iff_isIso_desc` are **not** here: they are statements
of the categorical interface with no formal scheme and no Tate hypothesis in them, and they go
beside `CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.exists_isIso_desc_of_iso` and
`CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.ofIso`, whose subject is exactly which characterisations of the
quotient are two-way. That is the disposition
`FormalSchemes.TateInvNodeChartDescent`'s implementation notes argued for and took for
`CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.exists_isIso_desc_of_iso` itself, at the same price:
`FormalSchemes.ActionQuotient` has reverse closure **96** — 95 before this file, which reaches
it — against this file's **7**.
`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.isIso_iff_isIso_base_and_isIso_c_app` goes beside the
one-way `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.isIso_of_isIso_base_of_isIso_c_app` in
`FormalSchemes.ActionQuotientRestrictQuotient` (reverse closure **16**, 15 before this file) for the
same reason and much more cheaply.

The two general statements that *are* here —
`CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.globalSectionsHom_desc_eq` and
`FormalSpectrum.isIso_c_app_top_of_bijective_globalSectionsHom` — have no existing home:
`FormalSchemes.GlobalSectionsHom` and `FormalSchemes.ActionQuotientSectionInjective` are
**import-incomparable**, neither being in the other's closure, with forward closures **42** and
**6** counted with the module itself; a home for the first would therefore be a new leaf at forward
closure **49** (48 modules besides itself). Each has one consumer, both in this file, so they are
kept here and that leaf should be cut when a second consumer appears, which is the standing
disposition on this tree for a general statement with a single consumer. This file's own forward
closure is **253** with itself, so a general statement parked here is reachable only at that
price.

`CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.injective_c_app` carries `HasCoproduct` and `HasCoequalizer`
instance hypotheses even though it is stated at an arbitrary presentation of the quotient — it is
proved by transporting the coequalizer case — so
`CategoryTheory.IsActionQuotient.globalSectionsHom_desc_eq` carries them too. They are discharged by
`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace`'s cocompleteness at every use below.

## References

* [Grothendieck, *Éléments de géométrie algébrique I*][EGA1], Ch. I, §10.4 (10.4.6), §10.6.
* [Deligne–Rapoport, *Les schémas de modules de courbes elliptiques*], II.1 — the Néron 1-gon.
-/

